{"abstract":[{"text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex. NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number_of_spanning_trees"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": counts pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). A dense Cholesky factorization of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Laplacian with one vertex removed, its pivots multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the result overflows only past ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s range, to ","type":"text"},{"code":".infinity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When every weight is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer (unweighted included) a result below 2⁵³ is rounded to the nearest integer, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then exact; nearer to 2⁵³ and above, it is within a relative 10⁻¹² or so, not exact. O(n³) time,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"n² ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees(weight:)-28jjs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)-28jjs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21numberOfSpanningTrees6weightSdqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_tSBRd__lF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blo